The task needs a genuine loop invariant, so `k-proof-technique` is now guiding the design. I’m using a simple exhaustive trial-divisor loop: after computing `max(start)` and `min(end)`, it scans every integer divisor from 2 through `length - 1`. That keeps the source within the translator’s subset and gives a direct invariant connecting the loop state to “a proper divisor has been seen.”
